    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Description\n\nI'm aware of similar old issues, but I don't think they made it clear enough\n\nSometimes when you're working in a project you want to look for your environment file to see some variables, but the underlaying cli by default will not show files ignored by git like ripgrep for example.\n\nYou may say that I can configure ripgrep to disable this option but that will make files  in vendor director for php and node_modules directory for javascript show in the results.\n\nIt does not have to be a builtin action, even a way to pass options to the underlaying cli through mini.pick will make do.\n\n(forgive my poor English)",
