            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nAllowing to passing CLI arguments to built-in  pickers is indeed the approach I'd like to avoid as much as possible to reduce complexity. This is described in #825 and #830.\n\nThe more or less reasonable way of having setup that can search through `.gitignore`d and/or hidden files is to use a dedicated CLI tool (like for `rigprep`, for example) config file for specific purposes. Something like this:\n- Create '~/.config/nvim/rg-config-hidden` file with `--hidden` and/or `--no-ignore` lines.\n- Cache the \"global\" value of `RIPGREP_CONFIG_PATH` environment variable.\n- Temporarily set `RIPGREP_CONFIG_PATH` environment variable to point to that config file.\n- Start picker that uses `rg`. It now should provide results based on the temporary config.\n- After picker is finished, reset `RIPGREP_CONFIG_PATH` back to its original value.\n\nHere is [one way to do it](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/1291#issuecomment-2423757112) (the `load_temp_rg` function and its usage).\n\nClosing as 1) duplicate; 2) \"already kind of possible\"; and 3) \"not planned\".",
